Current State
We have three components:
TFG
PCT
SFS Common
TFG and PCT currently have hardcoded project versions in their respective pom.xml files.
Example:
XML
<version>0.1.0</version>
SFS Common already uses a version property:
XML
<version>${sfs.common.version}</version>
Both TFG and PCT consume SFS Common as a dependency and reference:
XML
${sfs.common.version}
for resolving the SFS Common artifact version.
Requirement
We want TFG and PCT project versions to be dynamically controlled during build execution.
Instead of hardcoded project versions, the version should be supplied as a build parameter.
Example:
Bash
mvn clean install -Drelease.version=1.2.0
The supplied version should be used for:
Generated JAR artifacts
Generated TAR/Assembly artifacts
Maven project version metadata
Proposed Approach
Component Version
Replace hardcoded versions in TFG and PCT with:
XML
<version>${release.version}</version>
This allows the component version to be controlled externally during the build.
SFS Common Version
Continue using the existing approach:
XML
<version>${sfs.common.version}</version>
for the SFS Common dependency.
Expected Build Behavior
Build Command
Bash
mvn clean install \
  -Drelease.version=1.2.0 \
  -Dsfs.common.version=1.0.0
Result
Artifact
Version
TFG
1.2.0
PCT
1.2.0
SFS Common Dependency
1.0.0
Generated artifacts:
Plain text
tfg-1.2.0.jar
tfg-1.2.0.tar

pct-1.2.0.jar
pct-1.2.0.tar
while resolving:
Plain text
com.cls.sfs:sfscommon:1.0.0
as the dependency.
Version Strategy Going Forward
Two independent version variables will be maintained:
Variable
Purpose
release.version
Controls TFG and PCT artifact versions
sfs.common.version
Controls SFS Common dependency version
This allows:
Independent versioning of application components (TFG/PCT)
Independent versioning of the shared Common library
Flexible upgrades of SFS Common without forcing application version changes
Stakeholder Confirmation Required
Confirm that TFG and PCT should use release.version as their project/artifact version.
Confirm that SFS Common should continue to use sfs.common.version as an independent dependency version.
Confirm that build pipelines will supply both version parameters when required
